msgstr ""

#: library/stat.rst:196
msgid ""
"The interpretation of \"file size\" changes according to the file type.  For "
"plain files this is the size of the file in bytes.  For FIFOs and sockets "
"under most flavors of Unix (including Linux in particular), the \"size\" is "
"the number of bytes waiting to be read at the time of the call "
"to :func:`os.stat`, :func:`os.fstat`, or :func:`os.lstat`; this can "
"sometimes be useful, especially for polling one of these special files after "
"a non-blocking open.  The meaning of the size field for other character and "
"block devices varies more, depending on the implementation of the underlying "
"system call."
msgstr ""

